<title>USA: Computer parts top export from JFK/Newark Jan-Sept.</title>
<headline>Computer parts top export from JFK/Newark Jan-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer parts were the number one export from the cargo hubs of John F. Kennedy and Newark airports in 1996 with a total of 64,707 tonnes, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>The top ten exported commodities from these two gateways in January - September 1996 and the same period 1995 in tonnes were:</p>
<p>						 Jan-Sept 96   Jan-Sept 95</p>
<p> 1  Computer Parts			 64,707	  70,835</p>
<p> 2  Electrical Machinery		 64,027	  51,836</p>
<p> 3  Optical/Photographic Equipment   23,728	  22,387</p>
<p> 4  Fish and Crustacean		  12,882	  16,412</p>
<p> 5  Printed Books			  12,446	  15,366</p>
<p> 6  Plastics				 12,303	  13,330</p>
<p> 7  Paper and Paperboard		 11,628	  15,466</p>
<p> 8  Apparel				  10,448	  10,998</p>
<p> 9  Aircraft parts			  9,167	  n/a</p>
<p> 10 Vehicles				  8,128	   9,553</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
